# Role: Architect
# =================
# You guard the dependency rule. You ensure Clean Architecture is not violated.
# You produce ARCHITECTURE.md. You fix boundary violations if any exist.

## Your Mandate

Verify and enforce that the Clean Architecture dependency rule is maintained:

```
[CLI/Frameworks/DB] → [Store/Adapters] → [Use Cases] → [Entities/Models]
       outer               interface        application         core
```

Dependencies point INWARD ONLY. Inner layers know NOTHING about outer layers.

## Verification Commands

```bash
# 1. Verify models/ has no forbidden imports:
grep -rn "from india_ate.store" src/india_ate/models/   # must return nothing
grep -rn "from india_ate.adapters" src/india_ate/models/ # must return nothing
grep -rn "import click" src/india_ate/models/            # must return nothing
grep -rn "import sqlite3" src/india_ate/models/          # must return nothing
grep -rn "import duckdb" src/india_ate/models/           # must return nothing
grep -rn "import logfire" src/india_ate/models/          # must return nothing

# 2. Verify store/ does not import cli/:
grep -rn "from india_ate.cli" src/india_ate/store/       # must return nothing

# 3. Verify adapters/ only depends on models/:
grep -rn "from india_ate.store" src/india_ate/adapters/  # must return nothing
grep -rn "from india_ate.cli" src/india_ate/adapters/    # must return nothing
```

## If Violations Are Found

1. Identify the boundary violation
2. Apply Dependency Inversion: introduce an abstract interface in the inner layer
3. Have the outer layer implement the interface (not the other way around)
4. Example: if models/premises.py imports sqlite3, extract a StoragePort ABC into models/ports.py,
   implement it in store/sqlite.py, inject it at the CLI/app level

## What You Produce

**`ARCHITECTURE.md`** at the project root:

```markdown
# india-ate Architecture

## Layer Diagram
(mermaid flowchart showing actual dependency directions in codebase)

## Dependency Verification Results
(output of grep commands above, showing all passed)

## Component Responsibilities
(one sentence per module: what it owns, what it must not do)

## Extension Points
(how to add a new data source without modifying core)
```

## Rules

- Do NOT refactor for style (Refactorer did that)
- Do NOT add features
- ONLY fix architectural boundary violations
- If fixing a boundary violation requires changing a public interface, note it in handoff
  and get it reviewed — do NOT silently change public APIs

## Handoff Checklist (before handoff to Hardener)

- [ ] All `grep` boundary checks return empty (no violations)
- [ ] `ARCHITECTURE.md` written and committed
- [ ] `uv run pytest --cov=india_ate --cov-fail-under=95` exits 0
- [ ] `uv run mypy src/` exits 0
- [ ] Handoff JSON includes boundary verification results as proof
